ssed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 46.7%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.59"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":15.93,"default_fair_val":15.93,"premium_pct":453,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":27.7,"pe_forward":24.4,"pb_trailing":2.4,"pb_forward":2.2,"div_yield":0.84,"ps_ratio":10.4,"fcf_to_ev":5.89,"fcf_to_mcap":2.39,"liab_to_assets":46.7,"cash_to_assets":0.4,"current_ratio":0.59,"roe":8.5,"roa":4.5,"moat":{"ticker":"CP","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"CP 的品牌價值主要體現在其作為北美鐵路運輸關鍵節點的可靠性和效率聲譽。然而，鐵路運輸本質上是基礎設施服務，客戶對價格的敏感度相對較高，尤其是在有替代運輸選項時。雖然 CP 在特定航線上擁有一定的定價能力，但其品牌溢價空間不如消費品品牌顯著。其定價權受制於宏觀經濟、燃料成本以及與其他運輸方式的競爭。","comment_en":"CP's brand value lies in its reputation for reliability and efficiency as a critical node in North American rail transport. However, rail transport is fundamentally an infrastructure service where customers are relatively price-sensitive, especially when alternative transport options exist. While CP possesses some pricing power on specific routes, its brand premium is less pronounced than that of consumer goods brands. Pricing power is constrained by macroeconomics, fuel costs, and competition from other modes of transport."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"鐵路行業受到嚴格的政府監管，這構成了顯著的進入壁壘。CP 擁有營運特定鐵路線路的特許經營權，這些路線的建設和維護成本極高，使得新競爭者難以進入。監管環境雖然帶來合規成本，但也保護了現有營運商免受過度競爭。CP 在關鍵區域的營運許可和安全標準認證，構成了其受監管的護城河。","comment_en":"The railroad industry is subject to stringent government regulation, which creates significant barriers to entry. CP holds franchises to operate specific rail lines, the construction and maintenance of which are prohibitively expensive, making it difficult for new competitors to enter. While the regulatory environment imposes compliance costs, it also protects incumbents from excessive competition. CP's operating permits and safety standard certifications in key regions form its regulated moat."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"客戶轉換至其他運輸方式（如卡車）的成本極高。鐵路運輸涉及龐大的供應鏈整合，包括貨物裝卸、倉儲以及與其他運輸環節的銜接。一旦客戶與 CP 建立起穩定的運輸協議和物流網絡，轉換不僅需要重新談判合同，還可能涉及基礎設施的調整和時間成本的增加。這種深度綁定是其強大的護城河。","comment_en":"The cost for customers to switch to alternative transportation modes, such as trucking, is extremely high. Rail transport involves extensive supply chain integration, including freight handling, warehousing, and connections with other transport links. Once a customer establishes stable shipping agreements and logistics networks with CP, switching not only requires renegotiating contracts but may also involve infrastructure adjustments and increased time costs. This deep integration is a powerful moat."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"CP 的網絡效應體現在其連接北美主要經濟中心的廣泛鐵路線路網絡。隨著網絡的擴展和效率的提升（例如通過收購 Kansas City Southern），其為客戶提供的服務價值也隨之增加。更多的貨物通過 CP 運輸，可以帶來更大的規模經濟和更優的調度效率，進而吸引更多客戶。然而，這種網絡效應不如社交網絡或市場平台那樣直接和強烈。","comment_en":"CP's network effects are evident in its extensive rail network connecting major economic centers across North America. As the network expands and efficiency improves (e.g., through the acquisition of Kansas City Southern), the value of services offered to customers increases. More freight transported via CP can lead to greater economies of scale and better scheduling efficiency, attracting more customers. However, this network effect is less direct and potent than those seen in social networks or marketplaces."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"鐵路運輸具有顯著的規模經濟效應。CP 作為北美最大的鐵路公司之一，其龐大的運輸量和固定的基礎設施成本攤薄了單位運輸成本。相較於卡車運輸，鐵路在長距離、大宗貨物的運輸上具有顯著的成本優勢。通過持續的基礎設施投資和運營優化，CP 能夠維持其在成本上的領先地位。","comment_en":"Rail transport exhibits significant economies of scale. As one of North America's largest railroad companies, CP's vast transportation volumes and fixed infrastructure costs dilute its per-unit transportation costs. Compared to trucking, rail offers a substantial cost advantage for long-haul, bulk freight. Through continuous infrastructure investment and operational optimization, CP maintains its cost leadership."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"CP 擁有連接美國、加拿大和墨西哥的獨特地理資產，特別是通過收購 Kansas City Southern，打通了南北美洲的關鍵運輸走廊。這些鐵路線路穿越重要的工業區和港口，提供了其他運輸方式難以複製的戰略連接。其地理位置的稀缺性和戰略重要性，構成了難以逾越的壁壘。","comment_en":"CP possesses unique geographic assets connecting the United States, Canada, and Mexico, notably through the acquisition of Kansas City Southern, which established a critical transport corridor between North and South America. These rail lines traverse important industrial zones and ports, providing strategic connections that are difficult to replicate by other transportation modes. The scarcity and strategic importance of its geographic locations form an almost insurmountable barrier."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"CP 在運營效率方面表現出色，持續優化列車調度、軌道維護和貨物處理流程。通過採用先進技術和數據分析，公司能夠提高列車準點率、降低燃料消耗並減少閒置時間。這種持續的運營改進不僅降低了成本，也提升了客戶滿意度，是其維持競爭力的關鍵。","comment_en":"CP demonstrates strong operational efficiency, continuously optimizing train scheduling, track maintenance, and freight handling processes. By adopting advanced technologies and data analytics, the company enhances train punctuality, reduces fuel consumption, and minimizes idle time. These ongoing operational improvements not only lower costs but also increase customer satisfaction, serving as a key factor in maintaining its competitive edge."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"CP 在資本配置方面展現出審慎和戰略性的眼光。公司歷史上通過精明的收購（如 KCS）擴大了網絡，並持續投資於基礎設施升級以提高效率和安全性。同時，公司也注重股東回報，通過股票回購和股息支付來平衡增長與回報。其對資本的有效配置，支持了長期的價值創造。","comment_en":"CP exhibits prudent and strategic capital allocation. Historically, the company has expanded its network through astute acquisitions (like KCS) and consistently invests in infrastructure upgrades to enhance efficiency and safety. Concurrently, it focuses on shareholder returns, balancing growth with returns through share buybacks and dividend payments. Its effective capital deployment supports long-term value creation."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"由於高昂的轉換成本和 CP 提供的可靠、高效的運輸服務，客戶忠誠度相對較高。公司通過建立長期的運輸合同、提供定制化的物流解決方案以及維持高水平的服務質量來鞏固客戶關係。一旦客戶深度整合到 CP 的網絡中，其留存率通常很高。","comment_en":"Due to high switching costs and the reliable, efficient transportation services CP provides, customer loyalty is relatively high. The company solidifies customer relationships by establishing long-term shipping contracts, offering customized logistics solutions, and maintaining high service quality. Once customers are deeply integrated into CP's network, their retention rates are typically very strong."},"m10_durability":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"鐵路行業的基礎設施屬性、高進入壁壘以及 CP 在北美關鍵運輸走廊的戰略地位，賦予了其業務高度的持久性。儘管面臨經濟週期波動和行業監管，但其核心業務模式在可預見的未來將保持穩定。CP 的網絡和運營效率使其能夠抵禦短期衝擊，並在長期內持續產生價值。","comment_en":"The infrastructure nature of the railroad industry, high barriers to entry, and CP's strategic position in key North American transportation corridors grant its business a high degree of durability. Despite facing economic cycle fluctuations and industry regulations, its core business model is expected to remain stable for the foreseeable future. CP's network and operational efficiency enable it to withstand short-term shocks and continue generating value over the long term."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Canadian Pacific Kansas City (CP) 展現出一個典型的「收費橋」或「特許經營」式經濟護城河。其核心競爭優勢來自於高昂的基礎設施建設成本和嚴格的監管環境所形成的進入壁壘（M2, M5），以及客戶因供應鏈整合而面臨的極高轉換成本（M3）。獨特的地理網絡，特別是連接美、加、墨三國的關鍵運輸走廊（M6），使其成為北美物流不可或缺的一環。雖然品牌定價權（M1）和網絡效應（M4）相對溫和，但其卓越的運營效率（M7）和審慎的資本配置（M8）進一步鞏固了其市場地位。綜合來看，CP 擁有一個堅固且持久的護城河，能夠在長期內為股東創造穩定價值。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Canadian Pacific Kansas City (CP) exhibits a classic 'toll bridge' or 'franchise' style economic moat. Its core competitive advantages stem from high infrastructure construction costs and stringent regulatory environments creating barriers to entry (M2, M5), coupled with extremely high switching costs for customers due to supply chain integration (M3). The unique geographic network, especially the critical transport corridors connecting the US, Canada, and Mexico (M6), makes it an indispensable part of North American logistics. While brand pricing power (M1) and network effects (M4) are more moderate, its excellent operational efficiency (M7) and prudent capital allocation (M8) further solidify its market position. Overall, CP possesses a robust and durable moat, capable of generating stable shareholder value over the long term.","evidenceHash":"7c17430629a46b618f9a4789a66a220aa7637b2a6a0990b57adebf2678a1230c","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CP.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CP.png","website":"https://www.cpkcr.com","ceo":"Keith E. Creel","full_time_employees":"19687","description":"Specializing in railway freight transportation, Canadian Pacific Kansas City Ltd. operates an extensive rail network connecting Canada, the United States, and Mexico. The company, headquartered in Calgary, Canada, began its operations on June 22, 2001.","description_en":"Specializing in railway freight transportation, Canadian Pacific Kansas City Ltd. operates an extensive rail network connecting Canada, the United States, and Mexico. The company, headquartered in Calgary, Canada, began its operations on June 22, 2001.","description_zh":"**加拿大太平洋堪薩斯城有限公司 (Canadian Pacific Kansas City Ltd. - CP)**\n\n加拿大太平洋堪薩斯城有限公司（CP）是一家領先的鐵路貨運運輸公司，其核心業務聚焦於提供跨越加拿大、美國及墨西哥的廣泛鐵路運輸服務。公司總部位於加拿大卡加利，自2001年6月22日起營運。\n\nCP的營運模式建立在其龐大且整合的鐵路網絡之上，該網絡是其關鍵技術與競爭優勢所在。透過此網絡，公司能夠高效地運輸各類貨物，包括但不限於：農產品、能源產品（如煤炭、石油）、金屬礦產、汽車、工業品及消費品等。其主要業務板塊涵蓋了貨運服務的各個環節，從貨物攬收到最終交付，提供端對端的物流解決方案。\n\nCP的營運策略著重於優化運輸效率、降低營運成本，並透過技術創新（如先進的信號系統、車輛監控技術）來提升安全性和可靠性。公司致力於成為北美地區最安全、最可靠、最準時的鐵路運輸服務提供者，為客戶創造價值。","address":"7550 Ogden Dale Road S.E.","city":"Calgary","state":"AB","zip":"T2C 4X9","country":"CA","phone":"14033193591","full_address":"7550 Ogden Dale Road S.E., Calgary, AB T2C 4X9, CA","range_52w":"68.42-96.9","year_high":96.9,"year_low":68.42,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":68.42,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"Peverett Jane L","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":303,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"PAULL MATTHEW H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":393,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"DENHAM GILLIAN H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":283,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"TRAFTON GORDON T. II","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":373,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"Fatt William R.","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":319,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"Courville Isabelle","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":159,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"Baird John Russell","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":282,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"Reardon Andrew Fitzpatrick","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":626,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-05","name":"MacDonald Ubavka Rebecca","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":319,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2017-07-03","name":"Velani Nadeem","title":"officer: VP and CFO","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":13,"price":162.18,"total_val":0}],"stock_splits":[{"date":"2021-05-14","ratio":"5 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"},{"date":"2001-10-02","ratio":"2 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"},{"date":"1985-06-10","ratio":"3 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"}],"fmp_symbol":"CP","real_5y_prices":[],"historical_dcf_series":[],"name_en":"Canadian Pacific Kansas City Ltd.","expansion":{"status":"available","capturedAt":"2026-10-22T13:11:38.877Z","reason":null,"detailPath":"cache/us_companies/CP.json"}},"snapshot":null,"model":null}
